Now we have the flip-side.  James Donald follows a truth (momentum is
defined operationally) by a non-sequitur (momentum is not well-defined). 
Sorry, but the momentum of an electron may be well-defined or it may
not.  Depends on the circumstances (the experimental setup).

>, and it *does* have a well defined angular momentum.

