PS  There is a difference between conventional orbital angular momentum
and spin or 'intrinsic' angular momentum.  It lies not in their 
measurement or operational definition, as we've seen, but in its
visualisability.  Orbital angular momentum can be interpreted as
rotation of an extended system - eg the rotation of the merry-go round.
Spin or intrinsic angular momentum is a property of a non-extended
object that does not correspond to rotation.

